            <ArticleTitle>Synthesis and evaluation of 2-amido-3-carboxamide thiophene CB₂ receptor agonists for pain management.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>2604-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.bmcl.2012.01.121</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>SAR studies on a series of thiophene amide derivatives provided CB(2) receptor agonists. The activity of the compounds was characterized by radioligand binding determination, multiple functional assays, ADME, and pharmacokinetic studies. A representative compound with selectivity for CB(2) over CB(1) effectively produced analgesia in behavioral models of neuropathic, inflammatory, and postsurgical pain. Control experiments using a CB(2) antagonist demonstrated the efficacy in the pain models resulted from CB(2) agonism.</AbstractText>
